            "body": "Just did, with Vim 9.2. Same result there too:\n\n- Vim's default for `'startofline'` is actually on (Nvim defaults to off), so I tested all three: the default, explicit `set startofline`, and explicit `set nostartofline`.\n- All three land `gk` at the identical (still wrong) column. No difference between them.\n\nSo this isn't Nvim-specific, same behavior in stock Vim, and `'startofline'` doesn't affect it there either despite the differing default.",
